  "liner": {
   "body_md": "This 1996 recording captures the Mountain Goats performing thirteen songs at The Garage in London on March 20th [1]. The audio file, transferred by waylaid, runs for 38 minutes and has earned a 4/5 rating from two listeners [1]. It is the only archived recording of this specific show, which is the seventh of 467 in the archive’s collection for the band [4]. The setlist includes several tracks that are rare or unique to the archive, such as “You’ve Got The Sex,” which is the only archived performance of that song [1][4]. Other early-in-archive tracks include “Whole Wide World,” “Cheshire County,” “The Anglo-Saxons,” and “Fresh Berries For You” [1][4]. The performance also features “Going To Palestine,” “Seeing Daylight,” and “No, I Can’t,” all of which have limited archived histories [1][4]. Reviews of this specific recording note that while the audio quality is occasionally odd with popping and echo, it creates a neat vibe [2]. One listener praised the song choice and the storytelling seeds present in the performance [2]. Another review specifically highlighted how good “The Recognition Scene” sounds in this recording [3]. The set also includes “California Song,” “The Sign,” “Nine Black Poppies,” and “Going To Georgia” [1].",
